{"availability":"available","full":"portolan-sdi/stac-iceberg-extension","name":"stac-iceberg-extension","description":"STAC Extension for Apache Iceberg table access and versioning metadata","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":7,"forks":2,"created":"2026-04-01T13:03:53Z","updated":"2026-10-11T21:29:58Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://portolan-sdi.github.io/stac-iceberg-extension/","topics":[],"demo":"https://portolan-sdi.github.io/stac-iceberg-extension/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:35:15.823Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:35:15.823Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:35:15.823Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T11:15:11.662Z","stars":7,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-09T13:18:53.226Z","stars":7,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-12T13:35:15.823Z","stars":7,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Work in Progress — This extension is under active development. Field names, schema, and the extension URL may change before the first stable release.","This extension adds Apache Iceberg table metadata to STAC Collections, enabling clients to discover and connect to Iceberg tables for querying geospatial data via PyIceberg, DuckDB, Spark, or BigQuery.","A fair question is whether the connection fields belong in existing extensions. The Table extension has table:storageoptions (an fsspec-style keyword bag) and table:tables (named tables on a Collection), and the Storage Extension has storage:schemes for where asset files physically live. We defer schema and file-location metadata to those, and we do not re-declare the underlying data files. But none of them can express the Iceberg-specific facts a client needs to open a table, the catalog type, the REST prefix, the format version, the current snapshot id, and the partition spec. Keeping these…"],"features":["Field Name Prefix: iceberg","Extension Maturity Classification: Proposal"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/p